Screen
/ PlangOS's side of the screen. Host plang starts this (wsl … /opt/plang/plang Screen). The
/ browser draws into plang-screen, whose binary frames go straight to this app's output — the
/ pipe to host plang — untouched. Input from the host's screen comes down on stdin, one line
/ per event. Ends when the host closes the pipe.
/ The first page is the desktop; every app opens in a window of its own.
- browser.start(Url="file:///home/plang/desktop.html", Width=1920, Height=1080, ToOutput=true, OnWindow=goal.call(Name="Window"), OnMessage=goal.call(Name="Desktop")); variable.set(Name=%browser%, Value=%!data%)
- on input call Input
- stop %browser%

Input
- send %!data% to %browser%

Desktop
/ The desktop page asks: {"open": url} opens a window; {"window": "focus|minimize|…", "id"}
/ goes to the screen.
- set %asked% to %!data%
- if %asked.open%, call Open
- if %asked.window%, call Command

Open
- open window %asked.open% in %browser%

Command
- send %asked% to %browser%

Window
/ The screen says what happened to a window: the desktop's taskbar shows it.
- post %!data% to the page of %browser%
